Z||000002||84Bill||04-20-2001||07:11 PM||||Its your lockup solenoid there is a connector on the L/H side rear area near the bell housing (looking from behind the car) just disconnect it for now. The actual device is in the side cover (metal cover) kinda a pain to get to but a must fix eventually item. This link will explain everything<BR> <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/th125.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/th125.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 04-20-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000003||Phil||04-20-2001||07:14 PM||||Torque converter lock-up solenoid sounds like it's shot. To test -disconnect the wires (2 wire connecter I think) on the back side of the tranny. If the problem goes away replace the solenoid.||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||04-20-2001||07:20 PM||||exacry actually its a 4 wire connector with only 2 wires in it and the clasp on the bottom side||||reg||14
Z||000005||jhar1987||04-20-2001||09:05 PM||||thanks for the help! i seem to be learning something everyday which is what i had hoped would happen with this forum.thanks again jeff||||reg||1
